oon</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>rjkowitsch</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Hughes</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>McCarthy</surname><given-names>JEG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dynamics and porcessivity of 40S ribosome scanning on mRNA in yeast</article-title><source>Molec. Biol</source><volume>51</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>987</fpage><lpage>1001</lpage><year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="b9-cin-02-163"><label>[9]</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bertsch</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gurtin</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Hilhorst</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Peletier</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>On interacting populations that disperse to avoid crowding: The effect of a sedentary colony</article-title><source>J. Math. Biol.</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><year>1984</year></citation></ref><ref id="b10-cin-02-163"><label>[10]</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bowersox</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Sorgente</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chemotaxis of aortic endot helial cells in response to fibronectin</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>2547</fpage><lpage>2551</lpage><year>1982</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7083147</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-cin-02-163"><label>[11]</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burton</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hutson</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Permanence for nonautonomous predator-prey sys